//? Title: Thomas elimination: actual pivots, substitutions and discrete residuals
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A tridiagonal system needs only linear elimination and substitution work when
its pivots remain usable. Actual transformed rows and returned-solution
residuals retain the original49-point sine-forcing Poisson problem.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

At row i compute w=sub_i/diag_(i-1), then diag_i<-diag_i-w*super_(i-1) and
rhs_i<-rhs_i-w*rhs_(i-1). Substitute from the last row upward. This is Gaussian
elimination without pivoting. SPD or suitable strict diagonal dominance supplies
familiar sufficient conditions; an arbitrary nonsingular tridiagonal matrix may
still require pivoting. Actual zero pivots fail before division. O(n)
work/storage contrasts with dense elimination. Algebraic residual b-Ax measures
the returned discrete solve; the continuous sine error additionally contains
finite-difference discretization error and is not the same diagnostic.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/thomas_algorithm_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::thomas_trace({0, -1, -1}, {2, 2, 2}, {-1, -1, 0}, {1, 0, 1});
    std::print("| actual phase | row | multiplier | current pivot | transformed RHS | actual x |\n| --- | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} |\n",
                   s.backward ? "substitute" : "eliminate", s.row, s.multiplier,
                   s.pivot, s.rhs, s.value);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual three-row tridiagonal system");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual elimination rows",
                                     r.eliminations));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual solution {}", r.x));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/thomas_algorithm_tiny.svg");
}
```
