> API and interpretation

All four vector lengths and every supplied finite value are checked, including
unused boundary coefficients. Matching empty inputs return empty. The retained
fixture uses diagonal2/h^2, active off-diagonal-1/h^2 and forcing
pi^2*sin(pi*x), preserving the original scaling. Actual zero pivots and
nonfinite arithmetic fail; no numerical stability or forward-error certificate
is inferred solely from a small residual.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Thomas tridiagonal Gaussian elimination; recurrence and no-pivot assumptions
  stated above

